title: ScreenConnect Host Connecting to Reported Rogue-Client Attacker Infrastructure
id: 69465c8a-db75-4c28-afcb-7af59fffcde2
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects a host connecting to infrastructure Huntress and ConnectWise tied
    to the November 2026 ScreenConnect MSP campaign, in which stolen partner
    credentials and the Run Command feature were used to install rogue
    ScreenConnect clients across customer endpoints. Covered here are the
    reported relay 185.99.255.28, the dynamic-DNS C2 hosts newnewnew.gotdns.org
    and soxnewwork.homedns.org, the additional C2 cdn007-digitaldownloads.com,
    the secondary C2 sc.payproofkit.com (155.94.150.39) and the ns.mo7sen.dev
    stager. A hit means a managed endpoint is talking to attacker-held
    remote-access infrastructure, which survives removal of the abused
    extensions because the rogue clients are separate ScreenConnect instances.
references:
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/active-screenconnect-attacks-breach-msps-impact-dozens-of-organizations/
    - https://www.huntress.com/blog/rogue-screenconnect-installations
    - https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/advisories
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/12
tags:
    - attack.t1219
    - attack.t1199
logsource:
    category: network_connection
detection:
    selection_domain:
        DestinationHostname|endswith:
            - 'newnewnew.gotdns.org'
            - 'soxnewwork.homedns.org'
            - 'cdn007-digitaldownloads.com'
            - 'sc.payproofkit.com'
            - 'ns.mo7sen.dev'
    selection_ip:
        DestinationIp:
            - '185.99.255.28'
            - '155.94.150.39'
    condition: selection_domain or selection_ip
falsepositives:
    - Threat-intelligence research, sandbox detonation, URL or proxy scanners and analyst pivots that deliberately resolve the reported infrastructure
    - Re-registration of the dynamic-DNS hostnames (gotdns.org / homedns.org) by an unrelated party after the campaign is dismantled
level: high
